; Method-pointer lambdas (objfpc): a lambda wanted as an `of object` type
; has a Self of its own, the object of the method it is written in (that
; method must be an object's), or nil outside methods. It uses nothing of
; the routines around it.
; RUN: not %pcc --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/methodlambda/errors.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: errors.pas:21:8: error: a lambda can be a method pointer ('of object') only in an object's method, whose Self is its object, or outside methods (its object is nil)
; CHECK: errors.pas:30:27: error: this method-pointer lambda uses 'k' of the routine around it; it can use only its object's members, its parameters and what is declared at program or unit level
; CHECK: errors.pas:31:27: error: this method-pointer lambda uses 'local' of the routine around it; it can use only its object's members, its parameters and what is declared at program or unit level
; CHECK: errors.pas:32:8: error: this lambda has 2 parameters, but 'TCalc' is wanted here
; CHECK: errors.pas:34:5: error: assigning to 'TCalc' from incompatible type 'TPlain'
; CHECK: errors.pas:41:8: error: a lambda can be a method pointer ('of object') only in an object's method, whose Self is its object, or outside methods (its object is nil)
; CHECK: errors.pas:49:23: error: use of undeclared identifier 'Self'
; CHECK-NOT: error:
;
; RUN: %pcc --mode=objfpc --emit-ast %S/Inputs/methodlambda/ast.pas -o - | FileCheck --check-prefix=AST %s
; AST: FunctionDecl '$lambda1' : integer <12:8>
; AST: NameRefExpr 'k' field (self) : integer <12:27>
; AST: AddrOfExpr : function(integer): integer of object <12:8>
;
; The code: the lambda takes Self after the static link, as a method does;
; its value is {code, the Self where it is made}.
; RUN: %pcc --mode=objfpc --emit-llvm %S/Inputs/methodlambda/ast.pas -o %t.ll
; RUN: FileCheck --check-prefix=IR %s < %t.ll
; RUN: opt -passes=verify -disable-output %t.ll
; IR-LABEL: define internal void @pas.tthing.init(ptr %link, ptr %self)
; IR: %obj = load ptr, ptr %self.addr
; IR-NEXT: insertvalue { ptr, ptr } { ptr @"pas.tthing.init.$lambda1", ptr undef }, ptr %obj, 1
; IR-LABEL: define internal i32 @"pas.tthing.init.$lambda1"(ptr %link, ptr %self, i32 %x)
